{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' FiniteFiber/ActualStabilizerSupportCorner.lean; printf '\\\\n--- FF20 review ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,300p' history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF20-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md\"","aggregated_output":"import FiniteFiber.QuasilocalStateGNSInterface\nimport FiniteFiber.StabilizerFiniteFiber\n\n/-!\n# The support-corner theorem instantiated at the actual stabilizer model\n\nThis file connects three already checked layers of the package:\n\n* the **actual** finite full-Pauli local system of\n  `FiniteFiber.FullPauliDirectedLocalSystem` (finite region algebras\n  `finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F`, identity padding `localInclusion`, the actual\n  full-Pauli matrices `fullPauliRegionMatrix`, and the compatible finite\n  stabilizer states of a `FullPauliStabilizerSystem`);\n* the C-star/GNS interface of `FiniteFiber.QuasilocalStateGNSInterface`\n  (`QuasilocalEmbedding`, `QuasilocalStabilizerState`, their GNS vector\n  `Ω = W.gnsVector` and GNS representation `π_ω`);\n* the checked support-corner theorem\n  `FiniteFiber.stabilizerAverageSequence_supportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit`.\n\n## What is constructed here (unconditional)\n\nFor a `QuasilocalEmbedding Site A` the single quasilocal image\n`Q.wordElement a ∈ A` of a full-Pauli word is constructed and shown to be\n* region independent (`QuasilocalEmbedding.embed_eq_wordElement`),\n* multiplicative and unital, hence a group homomorphism\n  `QuasilocalEmbedding.wordHom : FullPauliWord Site →* A`.\n\nFor a `QuasilocalStabilizerState S Q` this gives the **actual** stabilizer\naction on the GNS space,\n`W.stabilizerAction : SelfAdjointFiniteGroupAction (H := W.GNS) (G := ↥S.group)`,\nwhose representing operators are the GNS images `π_ω(g)` of the actual Pauli\nstabilizers, are self-adjoint (from algebraic involutivity of the stabilizer\nsystem), and — this is proved, not assumed — **fix the GNS vector**\n(`QuasilocalStabilizerState.stabilizerRepresentation_gnsVector`).\n\nConsequently the local supports of any increasing sequence of finite subgroups\nof the actual stabilizer group form a decreasing sequence of projections in any\nvon Neumann algebra containing the represented local algebras, and they all fix\n`Ω`.  Neither the vanishing hypothesis `hfix` nor the projection/decrease\nhypotheses of the abstract theorem have to be assumed at this instantiation.\n\n## What remains conditional (stated as explicit hypotheses)\n\nThe main theorem\n`actualStabilizerSystem_supportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit`\nis **conditional**.  Its hypotheses are exactly the global inputs which the\npresent package does not construct:\n\n1. `Q : QuasilocalEmbedding Site A` — the completed quasilocal C-star algebra\n   with its faithful, padding-compatible, densely-imaged local embeddings;\n2. `W : QuasilocalStabilizerState S Q` — the global stabilizer state extending\n   the compatible finite local states, whose GNS data is then Mathlib's;\n3. `M` together with `hM` — a von Neumann algebra on the GNS space containing\n   the represented finite local algebras;\n4. `T : ℕ → Subgroup ↥S.group` with `Fintype` instances and monotonicity — the\n   exhausting sequence of *finite* local stabilizer subgroups, giving the\n   decreasing finite stabilizer supports;\n5. `hstrong` — strong convergence of those supports to `q` (or, in the\n   canonical variant, no hypothesis at all: the canonical strong limit is\n   used);\n6. `C : GNSOrbitConditions M q W.gnsVector` — the regional/complementary\n   commutation data, the dense product orbit (fullness), and traciality of the\n   compressed vector functional on corner elements.\n\n**No claim is made that 1–6 follow from the manuscript's short-range\ndefinition.**  In particular nothing here constructs `A`, `ω`, the strong limit\nof the supports for a concrete lattice, the dense product orbit, or corner\ntraciality; and no direct-integral or type classification statement is made.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe conclusion is the existing `SupportCornerConclusion M q Ω`, whose\n`central_witness` field is the manuscript's every-nonzero-central-summand\nfinite-projection statement: for every nonzero central projection `z` of `M`,\n`z * q` is a nonzero finite projection of `M` below `z`.  It is restated\nseparately as `actualStabilizerSystem_central_witness_of_gnsOrbit`, together\nwith the semifiniteness corollary.\n-/\n\nnamespace FiniteFiber\n\nopen scoped InnerProductSpace\n\nvariable {Site : Type*} [DecidableEq Site]\nvariable {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A]\n\n/-! ### The single quasilocal image of a full-Pauli word -/\n\nnamespace QuasilocalEmbedding\n\nvariable (Q : QuasilocalEmbedding Site A)\n\n/--\nThe quasilocal image in `A` of an algebraic full-Pauli word: the image of its\nfinite-region matrix on the finite region given by its own support.\n-/\nnoncomputable def wordElement (a : FullPauliWord Site) : A :=\n  Q.embed a.label.support (fullPauliRegionMatrix a.label.support a)\n\n/--\nRegion independence: on any finite region containing the support of the word,\nthe embedded finite-region matrix is the quasilocal image.\n-/\ntheorem embed_eq_wordElement (F : Finset Site) (a : FullPauliWord Site)\n    (ha : a.SupportedIn F) :\n    Q.embed F (fullPauliRegionMatrix F a) = Q.wordElement a :=\n  Q.embed_fullPauliRegionMatrix_eq a.label.support F ha a (Finset.Subset.refl _)\n\n@[simp] theorem wordElement_one : Q.wordElement (1 : FullPauliWord Site) = 1 := by\n  have hsupp : (1 : FullPauliWord Site).SupportedIn (∅ : Finset Site) := by\n    show (1 : FullPauliWord Site).label.support ⊆ (∅ : Finset Site)\n    change (0 : ProjectivePauliWord Site).support ⊆ (∅ : Finset Site)\n    simp\n  rw [← Q.embed_eq_wordElement ∅ 1 hsupp, fullPauliRegionMatrix_one, map_one]\n\n/-- The quasilocal image is multiplicative: the phases compose exactly. -/\ntheorem wordElement_mul (a b : FullPauliWord Site) :\n    Q.wordElement (a * b) = Q.wordElement a * Q.wordElement b := by\n  classical\n  set F : Finset Site := a.label.support ∪ b.label.support with hF\n  have hlabel : (a * b).label = a.label + b.label := rfl\n  have ha : a.SupportedIn F := Finset.subset_union_left\n  have hb : b.SupportedIn F := Finset.subset_union_right\n  have hab : (a * b).SupportedIn F := by\n    show (a * b).label.support ⊆ F\n    rw [hlabel]\n    exact Finsupp.support_add\n  rw [← Q.embed_eq_wordElement F a ha, ← Q.embed_eq_wordElement F b hb,\n    ← Q.embed_eq_wordElement F (a * b) hab, fullPauliRegionMatrix_mul F a b ha, map_mul]\n\n/-- The quasilocal images assemble into a group homomorphism. -/\n@[simps] noncomputable def wordHom : FullPauliWord Site →* A where\n  toFun := Q.wordElement\n  map_one' := Q.wordElement_one\n  map_mul' := Q.wordElement_mul\n\n/-- The quasilocal image of an involutive word is self-adjoint. -/\ntheorem isSelfAdjoint_wordElement (a : FullPauliWord Site) (ha : a * a = 1) :\n    IsSelfAdjoint (Q.wordElement a) := by\n  have hmat : IsSelfAdjoint (fullPauliRegionMatrix a.label.support a) :=\n    fullPauliRegionMatrix_isSelfAdjoint a.label.support a (Finset.Subset.refl _) ha\n  show star (Q.wordElement a) = Q.wordElement a\n  rw [wordElement, ← map_star]\n  exact congrArg (Q.embed a.label.support) hmat\n\nend QuasilocalEmbedding\n\n/-! ### The actual stabilizer action on the GNS space -/\n\nnamespace QuasilocalStabilizerState\n\nvariable [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A]\nvariable {S : FullPauliStabilizerSystem Site} {Q : QuasilocalEmbedding Site A}\nvariable (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState S Q)\n\n/--\nThe GNS representation of the actual global stabilizer group: the stabilizer\nword `g` acts by `π_ω(g)`, the GNS image of its quasilocal Pauli operator.\n-/\n@[simps] noncomputable def stabilizerRepresentation :\n    ↥S.group →* (W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS) where\n  toFun g := W.gnsRepresentation (Q.wordElement (g : FullPauliWord Site))\n  map_one' := by\n    show W.gnsRepresentation (Q.wordElement (1 : FullPauliWord Site)) = 1\n    rw [Q.wordElement_one, map_one]\n  map_mul' g h := by\n    show W.gnsRepresentation (Q.wordElement ((g : FullPauliWord Site) * h)) = _\n    rw [Q.wordElement_mul, map_mul]\n\n/-- Each represented stabilizer is self-adjoint, by algebraic involutivity. -/\ntheorem isSelfAdjoint_stabilizerRepresentation (g : ↥S.group) :\n    IsSelfAdjoint (W.stabilizerRepresentation g) := by\n  have hinv : (g : FullPauliWord Site) * (g : FullPauliWord Site) = 1 :=\n    S.involutive _ g.property\n  have h := Q.isSelfAdjoint_wordElement (g : FullPauliWord Site) hinv\n  show star (W.gnsRepresentation (Q.wordElement (g : FullPauliWord Site))) = _\n  rw [← map_star]\n  exact congrArg W.gnsRepresentation h.star_eq\n\n/--\n**The actual finite-group symmetry data.**  The global Pauli stabilizer group\nacting on the GNS space by self-adjoint operators; the local supports of its\nfinite subgroups are the manuscript's code-space projections.\n-/\nnoncomputable def stabilizerAction :\n    SelfAdjointFiniteGroupAction (H := W.GNS) (G := ↥S.group) where\n  representation := W.stabilizerRepresentation\n  selfAdjoint := W.isSelfAdjoint_stabilizerRepresentation\n\n@[simp] theorem stabilizerAction_representation (g : ↥S.group) :\n    W.stabilizerAction.representation g =\n      W.gnsRepresentation (Q.wordElement (g : FullPauliWord Site)) := rfl\n\n/--\n**The GNS vector is fixed by every actual stabilizer.**  This is proved from\nthe finite-stage deviation computation of the interface, not assumed.\n-/\ntheorem stabilizerRepresentation_gnsVector (g : ↥S.group) :\n    W.stabilizerRepresentation g W.gnsVector = W.gnsVector := by\n  have hmem : (g : FullPauliWord Site) ∈\n      (S.regionStabilizer (g : FullPauliWord Site).label.support).group :=\n    (S.mem_regionStabilizer_group_iff _ _).mpr ⟨g.property, Finset.Subset.refl _⟩\n  have h := W.gnsRepresentation_fullPauliRegionMatrix_gnsVector\n    ((g : FullPauliWord Site).label.support) ⟨(g : FullPauliWord Site), hmem⟩\n  rw [localRepresentation_apply, Q.embed_eq_wordElement _ _ (Finset.Subset.refl _)] at h\n  exact h\n\n/-- Every local support of the actual stabilizer action fixes the GNS vector. -/\ntheorem stabilizerAction_representation_gnsVector (g : ↥S.group) :\n    W.stabilizerAction.representation g W.gnsVector = W.gnsVector :=\n  W.stabilizerRepresentation_gnsVector g\n\n/-- Each represented stabilizer lies in any von Neumann algebra containing the\nrepresented finite local algebras. -/\ntheorem stabilizerRepresentation_mem {M : VonNeumannAlgebra W.GNS}\n    (hM : ∀ (F : Finset Site) (x : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F),\n      W.gnsRepresentation (Q.embed F x) ∈ M)\n    (g : ↥S.group) : W.stabilizerRepresentation g ∈ M := by\n  have h := hM ((g : FullPauliWord Site).label.support)\n    (fullPauliRegionMatrix ((g : FullPauliWord Site).label.support)\n      (g : FullPauliWord Site))\n  rwa [Q.embed_eq_wordElement _ _ (Finset.Subset.refl _)] at h\n\nend QuasilocalStabilizerState\n\n/-! ### The conditional support-corner theorem at the actual stabilizer model -/\n\nsection ActualModel\n\nvariable [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A]\nvariable {S : FullPauliStabilizerSystem Site} {Q : QuasilocalEmbedding Site A}\n\n/--\n**The conditional support-corner theorem for the actual full-Pauli stabilizer\nmodel.**\n\nInputs, all explicit: a consistent full-Pauli stabilizer system `S`; a\nquasilocal C-star completion `Q` of the actual finite local algebras; a global\nstabilizer state `W` extending the compatible finite local states, with its\nMathlib GNS data; a von Neumann algebra `M` on the GNS space containing the\nrepresented local algebras (`hM`); an increasing sequence `T` of **finite**\nsubgroups of the actual stabilizer group, whose averages are the decreasing\nlocal code-space supports; strong convergence of those supports to `q`\n(`hstrong`); and the GNS-orbit data `C` — regional commutation, dense product\norbit (fullness) and corner traciality.\n\nConclusion: the full `SupportCornerConclusion`, in particular that every\nnonzero central summand of `M` contains the nonzero finite projection `z * q`.\n\nThe theorem is conditional exactly in the inputs listed above; nothing else is\nassumed.  In particular the projection and decrease of the supports, and the\ninvariance of the GNS vector under them, are supplied by the model.\n-/\ntheorem actualStabilizerSystem_supportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit\n    (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState S Q) (M : VonNeumannAlgebra W.GNS)\n    (hM : ∀ (F : Finset Site) (x : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F),\n      W.gnsRepresentation (Q.embed F x) ∈ M)\n    (T : ℕ → Subgroup ↥S.group) [∀ n, Fintype (T n)]\n    (hmonotone : ∀ n m : ℕ, n ≤ m → T n ≤ T m)\n    {q : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS}\n    (hstrong : StronglyTendsTo (stabilizerAverageSequence W.stabilizerAction T) q)\n    (C : GNSOrbitConditions M q W.gnsVector) :\n    SupportCornerConclusion M q W.gnsVector :=\n  stabilizerAverageSequence_supportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit\n    W.stabilizerAction T\n    (fun _ s => W.stabilizerRepresentation_mem hM (s : ↥S.group))\n    hmonotone\n    (fun _ s => W.stabilizerAction_representation_gnsVector (s : ↥S.group))\n    hstrong C\n\n/--\nThe canonical-strong-limit form: the limit projection is *constructed* from the\ndecreasing actual stabilizer supports, so no convergence hypothesis is needed.\n-/\ntheorem actualStabilizerSystem_canonicalSupportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit\n    (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState S Q) (M : VonNeumannAlgebra W.GNS)\n    (hM : ∀ (F : Finset Site) (x : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F),\n      W.gnsRepresentation (Q.embed F x) ∈ M)\n    (T : ℕ → Subgroup ↥S.group) [∀ n, Fintype (T n)]\n    (hmonotone : ∀ n m : ℕ, n ≤ m → T n ≤ T m)\n\n--- FF20 review ---\n# FF20 live closeout adversarial review\n\n## Decision\n\n**Accepted at the packet's stated conditional scope.**  The downloaded\nAristotle archive is retained in quarantine as\n`FF20-stabilizer-support-corner-instantiation.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`5097660af857a567d1a2ef5a0f415a7377f358528459651af95d1c1246d548fb`) and\nwas extracted only under `FF20-extracted/`.  The only integrated source is\n`formalization_finite_fibers/FiniteFiber/ActualStabilizerSupportCorner.lean`,\nwhich is byte-identical to the candidate.  Remote metadata, source context,\nREADME/HANDOFF differences, and the remote summary's commit/push assertion\nwere not integrated.\n\n## Scope audit\n\nThe module connects the actual full-Pauli local system and FF19's conditional\nquasilocal/GNS interface to the already checked support-corner result.  It\nadds no axiom, `sorry`, `admit`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, or `implemented_by`\ndeclaration.  It does not modify the manuscript.\n\n### Proved in the live package\n\n- `QuasilocalEmbedding.wordElement`, `embed_eq_wordElement`, `wordElement_one`,\n  `wordElement_mul`, and `wordHom` give a region-independent unital\n  multiplicative image of a `FullPauliWord`.\n- `QuasilocalStabilizerState.stabilizerRepresentation`, `stabilizerAction`,\n  `isSelfAdjoint_stabilizerRepresentation`,\n  `stabilizerRepresentation_gnsVector`, and `stabilizerRepresentation_mem`\n  give the represented actual stabilizer action, its self-adjointness, GNS\n  vector invariance, and membership from the stated local-algebra containment.\n- `actualStabilizerSystem_supportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit` concludes\n  `SupportCornerConclusion M q W.gnsVector` from exactly\n  `W`, `M`, `hM`, finite `T`, `hmonotone`, `hstrong`, and\n  `C : GNSOrbitConditions M q W.gnsVector`.\n- `actualStabilizerSystem_canonicalSupportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit` has\n  the same inputs except that it uses the constructed decreasing strong limit\n  and therefore has no `hstrong` premise.\n- `actualStabilizerSystem_central_witness_of_gnsOrbit` restates the target:\n  for `hz : IsCentralProjection M z` and `hz_nonzero : z != 0`, it returns\n  `IsFiniteProjection M (z * q) /\\\\ z * q != 0 /\\\\ IsSubprojection (z * q) z`.\n- `actualStabilizerSystem_semifinite_of_gnsOrbit` is the corresponding\n  conditional `IsSemifinite M` corollary.\n\n### Still conditional / not proved\n\nThe theorem does not construct the quasilocal completion or global state\n(`Q`, `W`), the ambient regional von Neumann algebra and containment `hM`, an\nexhausting finite subgroup sequence `T`, a noncanonical strong-limit proof\n`hstrong`, or `GNSOrbitConditions` (in particular the regional/product-orbit\ndata, fullness, and corner traciality).  Thus it does **not** establish that\nthese inputs follow from the manuscript short-range condition; it also makes\nno direct-integral or type-III claim.  This is the packet-required conditional\ninstantiation, not a completion of the global model.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `lake build FiniteFiber.ActualStabilizerSupportCorner` -- passed.\n- `lake build` -- passed.\n- `lake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean` -- passed; existing audited declarations\n  report only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- `#print axioms` for every public FF20 definition/theorem -- only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder scan of the candidate module -- no matches.\n\n## Adversarial findings\n\nNo blocking finding.  The potential overclaim -- treating the FF19 interface\nor the GNS-orbit conditions as constructed consequences of a short-range\nmodel -- is avoided in both the declarations and module documentation.\nResidual mathematical risk is precisely the unconstructed global hypotheses\nlisted above; successful compilation does not discharge them.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"remote=history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF21-extracted/aristotle-finite_fiber-fs6ue_hb_aristotle; sed -n '361,760p' \\\"\"'$remote/FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction.lean\"; printf '\"'\\\\n--- imports delta ---\\\\n'; diff -u FiniteFiber.lean \\\"\"'$remote/FiniteFiber.lean\"; printf '\"'\\\\n--- live imports existing actual ---\\\\n'; rg -n \\\"ActualStabilizerSupportCorner|FiniteRange\\\" FiniteFiber.lean; printf '\\\\n--- candidate theorem index ---\\\\n'; rg -n \\\"\"'^(theorem|def|structure|noncomputable def|noncomputable instance) \" \"$remote/FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction.lean\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"remote=history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF21-extracted/aristotle-finite_fiber-fs6ue_hb_aristotle; sed -n '361,760p' \\\"\"'$remote/FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction.lean\"; printf '\"'\\\\n--- imports delta ---\\\\n'; diff -u FiniteFiber.lean \\\"\"'$remote/FiniteFiber.lean\"; printf '\"'\\\\n--- live imports existing actual ---\\\\n'; rg -n \\\"ActualStabilizerSupportCorner|FiniteRange\\\" FiniteFiber.lean; printf '\\\\n--- candidate theorem index ---\\\\n'; rg -n \\\"\"'^(theorem|def|structure|noncomputable def|noncomputable instance) \" \"$remote/FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction.lean\"'","aggregated_output":"    rintro a ⟨s, rfl⟩ b ⟨t, rfl⟩ _\n    exact FullPauliWord.commute_of_mem_phaseFreeZSubgroup\n      (zWord_mem_phaseFreeZSubgroup s) (zWord_mem_phaseFreeZSubgroup t)\n  generator_involutive := by\n    rintro a ⟨s, rfl⟩\n    exact zWord_mul_self s\n  no_negative_identity := by\n    intro hmem\n    have hle : Subgroup.closure (Set.range (zWord (Site := ℕ))) ≤\n        FullPauliWord.phaseFreeZSubgroup ℕ := by\n      rw [Subgroup.closure_le]\n      rintro a ⟨s, rfl⟩\n      exact zWord_mem_phaseFreeZSubgroup s\n    exact FullPauliWord.negativeIdentity_not_mem_phaseFreeZSubgroup ℕ (hle hmem)\n  enumerate := id\n  enumerate_surjective := Function.surjective_id\n  neighborhood := fun s => {s}\n  self_mem_neighborhood := fun s => Finset.mem_singleton_self s\n  generator_range := by\n    rintro a ⟨s, rfl⟩\n    exact ⟨s, zWord_support s⟩\n\n/-- The all-`Z` finite-range system has nontrivial finite local stabilizer\ngroups: the `Z` stabilizer at site `k` is local at every stage `n > k`. -/\ntheorem zWord_mem_natAllZ_localStabilizer {k n : ℕ} (hkn : k < n) :\n    (⟨zWord k, natAllZFiniteRangeSystem.generator_mem_group ⟨k, rfl⟩⟩ :\n        ↥natAllZFiniteRangeSystem.stabilizerSystem.group) ∈\n      natAllZFiniteRangeSystem.localStabilizer n := by\n  refine (natAllZFiniteRangeSystem.mem_localStabilizer_iff n _).mpr ?_\n  refine (zWord_support k).trans ?_\n  intro s hs\n  rw [Finset.mem_singleton] at hs\n  subst hs\n  exact (natAllZFiniteRangeSystem.mem_region_iff n s).mpr ⟨s, hkn, Finset.mem_singleton_self s⟩\n\n/-! ### The bundled operator-side output handed to FF20 -/\n\nvariable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n\n/--\n**The support-corner input data.**  A decreasing sequence `p` of projections of\n`M`, each fixing the unit vector `xi` and hence nonzero, together with its\nstrong limit `q`, which is again a projection of `M` fixing `xi` and nonzero.\n\nThis is exactly the geometric/operator-algebraic package which the abstract\nsupport-corner theorem consumes; the remaining `GNSOrbitConditions` are the\nanalytic inputs and are not part of it.\n-/\nstructure FiniteRangeSupportCornerData (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H)\n    (p : ℕ → H →L[ℂ] H) (q : H →L[ℂ] H) (xi : H) where\n  /-- The finite stages are a decreasing sequence of projections of `M`. -/\n  decreasing : DecreasingProjectionSequence M p\n  /-- Every finite stage fixes the distinguished vector. -/\n  stage_fixes : ∀ n : ℕ, p n xi = xi\n  /-- Hence every finite stage is nonzero. -/\n  stage_ne_zero : ∀ n : ℕ, p n ≠ 0\n  /-- The stages converge strongly to `q`. -/\n  tendsTo : StronglyTendsTo p q\n  /-- The limit is a projection of `M`. -/\n  q_projection : IsProjectionIn M q\n  /-- The limit fixes the distinguished vector. -/\n  q_fixes : q xi = xi\n  /-- Hence the candidate corner projection is nonzero. -/\n  q_ne_zero : q ≠ 0\n\nnamespace FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem\n\nvariable {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A]\nvariable (R : FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem Site) {Q : QuasilocalEmbedding Site A}\n\n/-- The represented local code-space support of the region `Γ_n`:\n`π_ω(P_{Γ_n})`, the average of the finite local stabilizer group. -/\nnoncomputable def supportProjection (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q)\n    (n : ℕ) : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS :=\n  stabilizerAverageSequence W.stabilizerAction R.localStabilizer n\n\ntheorem supportProjection_eq (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q) :\n    R.supportProjection W = stabilizerAverageSequence W.stabilizerAction R.localStabilizer :=\n  rfl\n\n/-- **The decreasing sequence of local code-space supports.**  It uses only the\nexhaustion and the increasing finite local stabilizer groups. -/\ntheorem supportProjectionSequence (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q)\n    (M : VonNeumannAlgebra W.GNS)\n    (hM : ∀ (F : Finset Site) (x : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F),\n      W.gnsRepresentation (Q.embed F x) ∈ M) :\n    DecreasingProjectionSequence M (R.supportProjection W) :=\n  stabilizerAverageSequence_decreasingProjectionSequence W.stabilizerAction\n    R.localStabilizer\n    (fun _ s => W.stabilizerRepresentation_mem hM (s : ↥R.stabilizerSystem.group))\n    R.localStabilizer_mono\n\n/-- Each local code-space support fixes the GNS vector. -/\ntheorem supportProjection_gnsVector (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q)\n    (n : ℕ) : R.supportProjection W n W.gnsVector = W.gnsVector :=\n  stabilizerAverageSequence_fixes W.stabilizerAction R.localStabilizer W.gnsVector\n    (fun _ s => W.stabilizerAction_representation_gnsVector\n      (s : ↥R.stabilizerSystem.group)) n\n\n/-- The GNS vector is nonzero, since it is a unit vector. -/\ntheorem gnsVector_ne_zero (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q) :\n    W.gnsVector ≠ 0 := by\n  intro h\n  have := W.norm_gnsVector\n  rw [h, norm_zero] at this\n  exact zero_ne_one this\n\n/-- Each local code-space support is nonzero: the code space contains `Ω`. -/\ntheorem supportProjection_ne_zero (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q)\n    (n : ℕ) : R.supportProjection W n ≠ 0 :=\n  stabilizerAverageSequence_ne_zero W.stabilizerAction R.localStabilizer\n    (R.gnsVector_ne_zero W)\n    (fun _ s => W.stabilizerAction_representation_gnsVector\n      (s : ↥R.stabilizerSystem.group)) n\n\n/--\n**The candidate corner projection.**  The strong limit of the decreasing local\ncode-space supports; it is *constructed* (as the canonical strong limit of\n`FiniteFiber.StrongSupport`), so no convergence premise is required.\n-/\nnoncomputable def cornerProjection (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q) :\n    W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS :=\n  decreasingProjectionStrongLimit (R.supportProjection W)\n\ntheorem stronglyTendsTo_cornerProjection\n    (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q) (M : VonNeumannAlgebra W.GNS)\n    (hM : ∀ (F : Finset Site) (x : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F),\n      W.gnsRepresentation (Q.embed F x) ∈ M) :\n    StronglyTendsTo (R.supportProjection W) (R.cornerProjection W) :=\n  (R.supportProjectionSequence W M hM).stronglyTendsTo_decreasingProjectionStrongLimit\n\ntheorem cornerProjection_isProjectionIn\n    (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q) (M : VonNeumannAlgebra W.GNS)\n    (hM : ∀ (F : Finset Site) (x : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F),\n      W.gnsRepresentation (Q.embed F x) ∈ M) :\n    IsProjectionIn M (R.cornerProjection W) :=\n  (R.supportProjectionSequence W M hM).decreasingProjectionStrongLimit_isProjectionIn\n\ntheorem cornerProjection_gnsVector\n    (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q) (M : VonNeumannAlgebra W.GNS)\n    (hM : ∀ (F : Finset Site) (x : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F),\n      W.gnsRepresentation (Q.embed F x) ∈ M) :\n    R.cornerProjection W W.gnsVector = W.gnsVector :=\n  (R.supportProjectionSequence W M hM).decreasingProjectionStrongLimit_fixes\n    (R.supportProjection_gnsVector W)\n\n/-- **The candidate corner projection is nonzero**, because it fixes the unit\nGNS vector. -/\ntheorem cornerProjection_ne_zero\n    (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q) (M : VonNeumannAlgebra W.GNS)\n    (hM : ∀ (F : Finset Site) (x : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F),\n      W.gnsRepresentation (Q.embed F x) ∈ M) :\n    R.cornerProjection W ≠ 0 := by\n  intro hzero\n  have hfix := R.cornerProjection_gnsVector W M hM\n  rw [hzero] at hfix\n  exact R.gnsVector_ne_zero W (by simpa using hfix.symm)\n\n/--\n**The main construction.**  From a countable locally finite lattice with a\nfinite-range consistent stabilizer system, a quasilocal completion `Q`, a\nglobal stabilizer state `W`, and a von Neumann algebra `M` containing the\nrepresented finite local algebras, the decreasing local code-space supports and\ntheir strong limit — a nonzero candidate corner projection fixing `Ω` — are\nconstructed.  No analytic hypothesis beyond `hM` enters.\n-/\nnoncomputable def supportCornerData\n    (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q) (M : VonNeumannAlgebra W.GNS)\n    (hM : ∀ (F : Finset Site) (x : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F),\n      W.gnsRepresentation (Q.embed F x) ∈ M) :\n    FiniteRangeSupportCornerData M (R.supportProjection W) (R.cornerProjection W)\n      W.gnsVector where\n  decreasing := R.supportProjectionSequence W M hM\n  stage_fixes := R.supportProjection_gnsVector W\n  stage_ne_zero := R.supportProjection_ne_zero W\n  tendsTo := R.stronglyTendsTo_cornerProjection W M hM\n  q_projection := R.cornerProjection_isProjectionIn W M hM\n  q_fixes := R.cornerProjection_gnsVector W M hM\n  q_ne_zero := R.cornerProjection_ne_zero W M hM\n\nend FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem\n\n/-! ### Feeding the construction to FF20 -/\n\nsection FiniteRangeModel\n\nvariable {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A]\nvariable (R : FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem Site) {Q : QuasilocalEmbedding Site A}\n\n/--\n**The support-corner theorem at a finite-range stabilizer system.**\n\nThe lattice geometry (exhaustion), the finite local stabilizer groups, the\ndecreasing local code-space supports, their strong limit `q`, its projection\nproperty, its invariance under the GNS vector and its nonvanishing are all\n*constructed* from the finite-range data.  The remaining hypotheses are exactly\nthe global analytic ones: the quasilocal completion `Q`, the state `W`, the\nalgebra `M` with `hM`, and the GNS-orbit conditions `C` (regional commutation,\ndense product orbit, corner traciality).\n-/\ntheorem finiteRange_supportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit\n    (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q) (M : VonNeumannAlgebra W.GNS)\n    (hM : ∀ (F : Finset Site) (x : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F),\n      W.gnsRepresentation (Q.embed F x) ∈ M)\n    (C : GNSOrbitConditions M (R.cornerProjection W) W.gnsVector) :\n    SupportCornerConclusion M (R.cornerProjection W) W.gnsVector :=\n  actualStabilizerSystem_supportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit W M hM\n    R.localStabilizer R.localStabilizer_mono\n    (R.stronglyTendsTo_cornerProjection W M hM) C\n\n/--\nThe manuscript's every-nonzero-central-summand statement at a finite-range\nstabilizer system: for every nonzero central projection `z` of `M`, the\ncompression `z * q` is a nonzero finite projection of `M` below `z`.\n-/\ntheorem finiteRange_central_witness_of_gnsOrbit\n    (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q) (M : VonNeumannAlgebra W.GNS)\n    (hM : ∀ (F : Finset Site) (x : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F),\n      W.gnsRepresentation (Q.embed F x) ∈ M)\n    (C : GNSOrbitConditions M (R.cornerProjection W) W.gnsVector)\n    (z : W.GNS →L[ℂ] W.GNS) (hz : IsCentralProjection M z) (hz_nonzero : z ≠ 0) :\n    IsFiniteProjection M (z * R.cornerProjection W) ∧ z * R.cornerProjection W ≠ 0 ∧\n      IsSubprojection (z * R.cornerProjection W) z :=\n  (finiteRange_supportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit R W M hM C).central_witness z hz\n    hz_nonzero\n\nend FiniteRangeModel\n\nend FiniteFiber\n\n--- imports delta ---\n--- FiniteFiber.lean\t2026-08-06 20:08:03.450925814 +0200\n+++ history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF21-extracted/aristotle-finite_fiber-fs6ue_hb_aristotle/FiniteFiber.lean\t2026-08-07 00:19:50.000000000 +0200\n@@ -30,3 +30,5 @@\n import FiniteFiber.FiniteStabilizerStateChain\n import FiniteFiber.SequentialLocalFunctional\n import FiniteFiber.CountablePauliRepresentation\n+import FiniteFiber.ActualStabilizerSupportCorner\n+import FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction\n\n--- live imports existing actual ---\n\n--- candidate theorem index ---\n107:structure FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem (Site : Type*) [DecidableEq Site] extends\n128:def region (n : ℕ) : Finset Site :=\n131:theorem mem_region_iff (n : ℕ) (s : Site) :\n136:theorem region_mono : Monotone R.region := by\n144:theorem neighborhood_subset_region (k : ℕ) :\n150:theorem mem_region (s : Site) : ∃ n, s ∈ R.region n := by\n155:def exhaustion : ProjectivePauliWord.FiniteExhaustion Site where\n161:theorem exists_region_superset (F : Finset Site) : ∃ n, F ⊆ R.region n :=\n169:theorem generator_supportedIn_region {g : FullPauliWord Site} (hg : g ∈ R.generators) :\n178:noncomputable def stabilizerSystem : FullPauliStabilizerSystem Site where\n187:theorem generator_mem_group {g : FullPauliWord Site} (hg : g ∈ R.generators) :\n192:theorem stabilizerSystem_commute (g h : R.stabilizerSystem.group) :\n202:noncomputable def localStabilizer (n : ℕ) : Subgroup ↥R.stabilizerSystem.group :=\n206:theorem mem_localStabilizer_iff (n : ℕ) (g : ↥R.stabilizerSystem.group) :\n215:theorem localStabilizer_mono (n m : ℕ) (hnm : n ≤ m) :\n223:theorem exists_mem_localStabilizer (g : ↥R.stabilizerSystem.group) :\n229:theorem iSup_localStabilizer : (⨆ n : ℕ, R.localStabilizer n) = ⊤ := by\n235:theorem generator_mem_localStabilizer {g : FullPauliWord Site} (hg : g ∈ R.generators) :\n242:noncomputable instance localStabilizerFintype (n : ℕ) :\n272:def LocallyGenerated : Prop :=\n278:theorem closure_localGenerators_le_regionStabilizer (n : ℕ) :\n294:def phaseFreeZSubgroup (Site : Type*) : Subgroup (FullPauliWord Site) where\n316:theorem mem_phaseFreeZSubgroup_iff {Site : Type*} (a : FullPauliWord Site) :\n321:theorem commute_of_mem_phaseFreeZSubgroup {Site : Type*} {a b : FullPauliWord Site}\n337:theorem negativeIdentity_not_mem_phaseFreeZSubgroup (Site : Type*) :\n347:theorem zWord_mem_phaseFreeZSubgroup (s : Site) :\n358:noncomputable def natAllZFiniteRangeSystem : FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem ℕ where\n385:theorem zWord_mem_natAllZ_localStabilizer {k n : ℕ} (hkn : k < n) :\n409:structure FiniteRangeSupportCornerData (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H)\n433:noncomputable def supportProjection (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q)\n437:theorem supportProjection_eq (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q) :\n443:theorem supportProjectionSequence (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q)\n454:theorem supportProjection_gnsVector (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q)\n461:theorem gnsVector_ne_zero (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q) :\n469:theorem supportProjection_ne_zero (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q)\n481:noncomputable def cornerProjection (W : QuasilocalStabilizerState R.stabilizerSystem Q) :\n485:theorem stronglyTendsTo_cornerProjection\n492:theorem cornerProjection_isProjectionIn\n499:theorem cornerProjection_gnsVector\n509:theorem cornerProjection_ne_zero\n527:noncomputable def supportCornerData\n561:theorem finiteRange_supportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit\n576:theorem finiteRange_central_witness_of_gnsOrbit\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
